# LF in every text file, on every platform. Byte-exact content is part of what is tested
# and shipped: the bundled vocabularies are pinned by checksum in their catalog, and the
# expected reports are compared byte for byte. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf
# would otherwise rewrite them all as CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The bundled vocabularies are upstream files, kept byte for byte as published (some with
# CRLF) because the catalog pins their checksums. Never convert them.
src/ontolint/vocabularies/*.ttl -text
